            <article class="markdown-body entry-content container-lg" itemprop="text"><h2 dir="auto"><a id="user-content-follow-redirects" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#follow-redirects"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Follow Redirects</h2>
<p dir="auto">Drop-in replacement for Node's <code>http</code> and <code>https</code> modules that automatically follows redirects.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/follow-redirects" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/6494fb045ba4e6512c9fb32e8c68f46d16867b9c3802b81b7c6f68bbb5899f12/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6e706d2f762f666f6c6c6f772d7265646972656374732e737667" alt="npm version" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/npm/v/follow-redirects.svg" style="max-width: 100%;"></a>
<a href="https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/actions"><img src="https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/workflows/CI/badge.svg" alt="Build Status" style="max-width: 100%;"></a>
<a href="https://coveralls.io/r/follow-redirects/follow-redirects?branch=master" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/94b9d5aa164f2ef65ef68f8434446c45a5ffead8fb3a13a62f7085b030614474/68747470733a2f2f636f766572616c6c732e696f2f7265706f732f666f6c6c6f772d7265646972656374732f666f6c6c6f772d7265646972656374732f62616467652e7376673f6272616e63683d6d6173746572" alt="Coverage Status" data-canonical-src="https://coveralls.io/repos/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/badge.svg?branch=master" style="max-width: 100%;"></a>
<a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/follow-redirects" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/fc81d2fea4f24acbad2fe7e81d004f43fead1cc54c92e6b27656f8ef1f3b3214/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6e706d2f646d2f666f6c6c6f772d7265646972656374732e737667" alt="npm downloads" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/follow-redirects.svg" style="max-width: 100%;"></a>
<a href="https://github.com/sponsors/RubenVerborgh"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/2d9869d2c05750e57a68483ad270b4890663b3d2b4e042b5caf8ae8df0906b3c/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f7374617469632f76313f6c6162656c3d53706f6e736f72266d6573736167653d254630253946253932253936266c6f676f3d476974487562" alt="Sponsor on GitHub" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/static/v1?label=Sponsor&amp;message=%F0%9F%92%96&amp;logo=GitHub" style="max-width: 100%;"></a></p>
<p dir="auto"><code>follow-redirects</code> provides <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_http_request_options_callback" rel="nofollow">request</a> and <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_http_get_options_callback" rel="nofollow">get</a>
methods that behave identically to those found on the native <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_http_request_options_callback" rel="nofollow">http</a> and <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/https.html#https_https_request_options_callback" rel="nofollow">https</a>
modules, with the exception that they will seamlessly follow redirects.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const { http, https } = require('follow-redirects');

http.get('http://bit.ly/900913', response =&gt; {
  response.on('data', chunk =&gt; {
    console.log(chunk);
  });
}).on('error', err =&gt; {
  console.error(err);
});"><pre><span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span> http<span class="pl-kos">,</span> https <span class="pl-kos">}</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'follow-redirects'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>

<span class="pl-s1">http</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">get</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'http://bit.ly/900913'</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span> <span class="pl-s1">response</span> <span class="pl-c1">=&gt;</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class="pl-s1">response</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">on</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'data'</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span> <span class="pl-s1">chunk</span> <span class="pl-c1">=&gt;</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span>
    <span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">log</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">chunk</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
  <span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">on</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'error'</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span> <span class="pl-s1">err</span> <span class="pl-c1">=&gt;</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">error</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">err</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">You can inspect the final redirected URL through the <code>responseUrl</code> property on the <code>response</code>.
If no redirection happened, <code>responseUrl</code> is the original request URL.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const request = https.request({
  host: 'bitly.com',
  path: '/UHfDGO',
}, response =&gt; {
  console.log(response.responseUrl);
  // 'http://duckduckgo.com/robots.txt'
});
request.end();"><pre><span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">request</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-s1">https</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">request</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class="pl-c1">host</span>: <span class="pl-s">'bitly.com'</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span>
  <span class="pl-c1">path</span>: <span class="pl-s">'/UHfDGO'</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span>
<span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span> <span class="pl-s1">response</span> <span class="pl-c1">=&gt;</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">log</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">response</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">responseUrl</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
  <span class="pl-c">// 'http://duckduckgo.com/robots.txt'</span>
<span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-s1">request</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">end</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span></pre></div>
<h2 dir="auto"><a id="user-content-options" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#options"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Options</h2>
<h3 dir="auto"><a id="user-content-global-options" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#global-options"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Global options</h3>
<p dir="auto">Global options are set directly on the <code>follow-redirects</code> module:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const followRedirects = require('follow-redirects');
followRedirects.maxRedirects = 10;
followRedirects.maxBodyLength = 20 * 1024 * 1024; // 20 MB"><pre><span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">followRedirects</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'follow-redirects'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-s1">followRedirects</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">maxRedirects</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-c1">10</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-s1">followRedirects</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">maxBodyLength</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-c1">20</span> <span class="pl-c1">*</span> <span class="pl-c1">1024</span> <span class="pl-c1">*</span> <span class="pl-c1">1024</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span> <span class="pl-c">// 20 MB</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">The following global options are supported:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto"><code>maxRedirects</code> (default: <code>21</code>) – sets the maximum number of allowed redirects; if exceeded, an error will be emitted.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><code>maxBodyLength</code> (default: 10MB) – sets the maximum size of the request body; if exceeded, an error will be emitted.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto"><a id="user-content-per-request-options" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#per-request-options"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Per-request options</h3>
<p dir="auto">Per-request options are set by passing an <code>options</code> object:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const url = require('url');
const { http, https } = require('follow-redirects');

const options = url.parse('http://bit.ly/900913');
options.maxRedirects = 10;
options.beforeRedirect = (options, { headers }) =&gt; {
  // Use this to adjust the request options upon redirecting,
  // to inspect the latest response headers,
  // or to cancel the request by throwing an error
  if (options.hostname === &quot;example.com&quot;) {
    options.auth = &quot;user:password&quot;;
  }
};
http.request(options);"><pre><span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">url</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'url'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span> http<span class="pl-kos">,</span> https <span class="pl-kos">}</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'follow-redirects'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>

<span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">options</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-s1">url</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">parse</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'http://bit.ly/900913'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-s1">options</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">maxRedirects</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-c1">10</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-s1">options</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">beforeRedirect</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">options</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span> headers <span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span> <span class="pl-c1">=&gt;</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class="pl-c">// Use this to adjust the request options upon redirecting,</span>
  <span class="pl-c">// to inspect the latest response headers,</span>
  <span class="pl-c">// or to cancel the request by throwing an error</span>
  <span class="pl-k">if</span> <span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">options</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">hostname</span> <span class="pl-c1">===</span> <span class="pl-s">"example.com"</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span>
    <span class="pl-s1">options</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">auth</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-s">"user:password"</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
  <span class="pl-kos">}</span>
<span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-s1">http</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">request</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s1">options</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">In addition to the <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_http_request_options_callback" rel="nofollow">standard HTTP</a> and <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/https.html#https_https_request_options_callback" rel="nofollow">HTTPS options</a>,
the following per-request options are supported:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto"><code>followRedirects</code> (default: <code>true</code>) – whether redirects should be followed.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><code>maxRedirects</code> (default: <code>21</code>) – sets the maximum number of allowed redirects; if exceeded, an error will be emitted.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><code>maxBodyLength</code> (default: 10MB) – sets the maximum size of the request body; if exceeded, an error will be emitted.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><code>beforeRedirect</code> (default: <code>undefined</code>) – optionally change the request <code>options</code> on redirects, or abort the request by throwing an error.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><code>agents</code> (default: <code>undefined</code>) – sets the <code>agent</code> option per protocol, since HTTP and HTTPS use different agents. Example value: <code>{ http: new http.Agent(), https: new https.Agent() }</code></p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><code>trackRedirects</code> (default: <code>false</code>) – whether to store the redirected response details into the <code>redirects</code> array on the response object.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto"><a id="user-content-advanced-usage" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#advanced-usage"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Advanced usage</h3>
<p dir="auto">By default, <code>follow-redirects</code> will use the Node.js default implementations
of <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/http.html" rel="nofollow"><code>http</code></a>
and <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/https.html" rel="nofollow"><code>https</code></a>.
To enable features such as caching and/or intermediate request tracking,
you might instead want to wrap <code>follow-redirects</code> around custom protocol implementations:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const { http, https } = require('follow-redirects').wrap({
  http: require('your-custom-http'),
  https: require('your-custom-https'),
});"><pre><span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-kos">{</span> http<span class="pl-kos">,</span> https <span class="pl-kos">}</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'follow-redirects'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">wrap</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class="pl-c1">http</span>: <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'your-custom-http'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span>
  <span class="pl-c1">https</span>: <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'your-custom-https'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">,</span>
<span class="pl-kos">}</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">Such custom protocols only need an implementation of the <code>request</code> method.</p>
<h2 dir="auto"><a id="user-content-browser-usage" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#browser-usage"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Browser Usage</h2>
<p dir="auto">Due to the way the browser works,
the <code>http</code> and <code>https</code> browser equivalents perform redirects by default.</p>
<p dir="auto">By requiring <code>follow-redirects</code> this way:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const http = require('follow-redirects/http');
const https = require('follow-redirects/https');"><pre><span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">http</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'follow-redirects/http'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">https</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-en">require</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">'follow-redirects/https'</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">you can easily tell webpack and friends to replace
<code>follow-redirect</code> by the built-in versions:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="{
  &quot;follow-redirects/http&quot;  : &quot;http&quot;,
  &quot;follow-redirects/https&quot; : &quot;https&quot;
}"><pre>{
  <span class="pl-ent">"follow-redirects/http"  </span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>http<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>,
  <span class="pl-ent">"follow-redirects/https" </span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>https<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
}</pre></div>
<h2 dir="auto"><a id="user-content-contributing" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#contributing"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Contributing</h2>
<p dir="auto">Pull Requests are always welcome. Please <a href="https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/issues">file an issue</a>
detailing your proposal before you invest your valuable time. Additional features and bug fixes should be accompanied
by tests. You can run the test suite locally with a simple <code>npm test</code> command.</p>
<h2 dir="auto"><a id="user-content-debug-logging" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" href="#debug-logging"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Debug Logging</h2>
<p dir="auto"><code>follow-redirects</code> uses the excellent <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/debug" rel="nofollow">debug</a> for logging. To turn on logging
set the environment variable <code>DEBUG=follow-redirects</code> for debug output from just this module. When running the test
suite it is sometimes advantageous to set <code>DEBUG=*</code> to see output from the express server as well.</p>
